  "summary": "ACAN (aggrecan) on chromosome 1, a dwarfism locus with five variant alleles. A horse is a dwarf when it has no working copy left, so two different variant alleles together still count. One pairing (D1/D1) is lethal at birth; every other such combination is a surviving dwarf. A horse with one variant copy is not a dwarf, but heterozygotes are reported to be shorter than horses with none.",
